y steed and  like the other albinorics she excelled  in her archery through her capabilities  she sought to find a place where the  albinourics would be free from the  oppression they receive  she and those able-bodied albinorics  would travel far north to the hidden  lands of the heilig tree  a land where those who have no place in  the lands between are welcome  under the banner of unalloyed gold  within the service of lord mikala  loretta would be able to secure passage  and a place for the albanorics but for  reasons unknown she could not journey  herself to retrieve her fellows  instead this task was given to a young  albanoric named latina and from the  consecrated snow fields she would  journey to lyrnia towards the village of  the albinorics  the tennis goal within the village would  be an item known as the birthing droplet  likely an item that is akin to the  primordial jew to which the albanorics  were created from  it was likely safeguarded within the  village to ensure the future of their  people should loretta's quest have  failed but now that it had succeeded the  droplet must now be transported to the  hailing tree  however their journey does not go as  planned the village is attacked by ensha  who was under the employ of the all  hearing one or the tarnished known as  serginian ofnir  together with a depraved perfumer and an  open killer ansha would lay waste to the  village killing many and driving those  that survived to utter madness  all in an attempt to acquire a sacred  medallion that would lead them to  michela's hailing tree  lieutenant would flee from the village  and hide within a cave but she would be  followed by ensha in a bloodhound night  where her wolf lobo would be killed  seeing she did not have the medallion on  her they leave her alive probably to  extract information later on as without  her wolf she could go nowhere  as a side note i don't know if this is  an oversight or  something intentional but the corpses  within this village are  commoners and not albinorics if you  attack them they bleed red instead of  white  so i'm not sure if this was intentional  that  the albanorics and the village bleed red  or  if maybe their blood doesn't turn white  until later on in their life but  i'm stumped on this one  this is where we the tarnished who would  be lord would come in  armed with information from a finger  reader we would know where to find the  albanoric who wielded michela's favor  within a pot we would find old albus  as per the instruction of the finger  reader we take pity on him and he  entrusts the first half of the medallion  to us  but whether by injuries or simply the  end he would perish before us  leaving us questioning where the other  half could be  upon defeating ensha and confronting  gideon though he would tell us to seek  latina within the lakeside cave  and when we meet her she would  understandably be angry  but after showing her the medallion and  explaining the situation she would come  to trust us  and she asks that we do her a great  service of escorting her back to the  consecrated snow fields  in exchange she would tell us the  location of the second half of the  medallion  as the brave tarnish that we are we  accept her offer and journey towards the  second half of the medallion towards  castle seoul  now oddly enough there are albanorics  within the castle soul but all of them  have been driven mad and seem to have  been tortured they are used as an alarm  system at which the ghosts of the  knights of seoul would appear  but after exterminating this area of the  ghost and its commander we would find  the second half of the medallion here at  the top of the castle  upon reaching the consecrated snow  fields latent would beckon us to go past  the town of ordina  towards the apostate derelict and within  we would find an albinouric who towers  over them  one who is named philia and within her  lateness surrenders the birthing droplet  oh young yet towering sister 